# Line endings.
#
# Every blob in this repo is stored LF. Git for Windows ships with
# core.autocrlf=true, so a checkout there rewrites files as CRLF. That is
# harmless for JS, CSS and HTML, but fatal for a shell script: the shebang
# becomes `#!/bin/sh\r`, which will not execute. The pre-commit hook would
# then stop running, silently taking the test gate and the SHELL_VERSION
# cache bump with it -- the same class of failure as F38, and just as quiet.
#
# So pin anything that has to run as a script to LF on every platform.

.githooks/** text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
